course: dictionary
lesson: 3262
title: Words for places on the map
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Equatorial is an adjective, a describing word. It describes things linked to the equator, the imaginary line around the middle of the Earth. Places near that line are equatorial.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «The goliath frog of Cameroon and Equatorial Guinea is the biggest frog in the world.» The capital E tells you Equatorial Guinea is the name of a place, and it is a country near the equator.
explain: Equatorial can also describe the weather. «Equatorial rainforest» and «equatorial climate» describe what a place is like: hot and often wet all year. To check, swap your meaning into the phrase. Does «hot and often wet all year rainforest» make sense? Then you have it.
fact: Equatorial is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as a rainforest or a climate.
fact: The equator is an imaginary line around the middle of the Earth.
fact: Equatorial areas are hot and often wet all year, and the temperature and day length stay almost the same all year.
fact: Ecuador, Kenya and Indonesia all have equatorial areas.
fact: «The goliath frog of Cameroon and Equatorial Guinea is the biggest frog in the world», about 32 centimetres long and over 3 kilograms.
exercise: Which phrase names a hot, wet place near the middle of the Earth? | polar ice cap | desert sand dune | mountain snowfield | *equatorial rainforest
exercise: What is the equator? | A river that flows into the sea | A kind of rainforest animal | *An imaginary line around the middle of the Earth | A tall mountain in Kenya
exercise: «The goliath frog of Cameroon and Equatorial Guinea is the biggest frog in the world.» What does the capital E in Equatorial Guinea tell you? | *It is the name of a place | It is a typing mistake | It starts a new sentence | It means the frog is very big
test: Which country in this lesson has equatorial areas? | Iceland | Norway | Canada | *Ecuador
test: What is the climate like in an equatorial region? | Cold and dry all year | *Hot and often wet all year | Windy and cool all year | Snowy in winter only
exam: Which meaning fits «equatorial rainforest»? | Very old and ruined | Cold and icy, near the North Pole | Dry sand and dunes, with no rain | *Hot and often wet, near the equator
